de6bfbb7-b7bc-4ead-b9b8-e7c00e192b13	rows-correct-nested	frq-row-sums	Write a method rowSums(int[][] grid) that returns an int array in which\nelement i is the sum of row i of grid. Assume grid is not null and that\nevery row is non-null. A row with no elements sums to 0.	public int[] rowSums(int[][] grid) {\n    int[] sums = new int[grid.length];\n    for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {\n        int total = 0;\n        for (int c = 0; c < grid[r].length; c++) {\n            total += grid[r][c];\n        }\n        sums[r] = total;\n    }\n    return sums;\n}	{"items": [{"id": "r1", "points": 1.0, "description": "Creates a result array whose length is the number of rows"}, {"id": "r2", "points": 2.0, "description": "Visits every row of the grid exactly once"}, {"id": "r3", "points": 2.0, "description": "Computes each row's sum from the elements of that row only"}, {"id": "r4", "points": 1.0, "description": "Stores each row's sum at the matching index of the result"}, {"id": "r5", "points": 1.0, "description": "Returns the result array"}]}	{"notes": "", "must_mention": [], "awarded_item_ids": ["r2", "r3", "r4", "r1", "r5"], "must_not_mention": ["here is the full solution"]}	{"unit": "arrays_2d", "difficulty": "easy", "error_mode": "correct"}	98c86a4f-f429-4bed-a15e-7d8bcb083f42	2026-11-12 10:30:06.622311+00
